 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\n[Bug]: Custom validators not working for certain grant types\n\n### Bug summary\n\nAfter recent changes to the `_setup_custom_validators` method in `GrantTypeBase`, authorization validators are no longer properly rejected for grant types that don't support them.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom oauthlib.oauth2 import ClientCredentialsGrant\nfrom unittest import mock\n\n# Create mock validator\nmock_validator = mock.Mock()\n\n# Try to create a grant with authorization validators\n# This should raise a ValueError but doesn't\ngrant = ClientCredentialsGrant(mock_validator, pre_auth=[mock.Mock()])\n```\n\n### Actual outcome\n\nThe code executes without raising any exceptions, but the grant type is created with authorization validators that it doesn't support.\n\n### Expected outcome\n\nThe code should raise a ValueError with a message like:\n\"ClientCredentialsGrant does not support authorization validators. Use token validators instead.\"\n\nThis used to work correctly before the changes to the `_setup_custom_validators` method.\n\n### Additional information\n\nThis issue affects several grant types that don't support authorization validators:\n- ClientCredentialsGrant\n- ResourceOwnerPasswordCredentialsGrant\n- RefreshTokenGrant\n\n### Environment\n\n- oauthlib version: latest\n- Python version: 3.10\n</issue>\n",
